---
title: AdviseCare - Sequence Diagram SD-15 - Emergency Access Request and Decision
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor ST as Staff member
    actor STW as Data Protection Steward
    participant W as Web App
    participant C as EmergencyAccessRequestsController
    participant S as EmergencyAccessRequestService
    participant N as INotificationService
    participant R as IGenericRepository
    participant DB as SQL Server
    ST->>W: Request emergency access to a student with a justification
    W->>C: POST /api/EmergencyAccessRequests {studentId, justification}
    C->>S: CreateAsync(CreatorId, request)
    S->>R: CreateAsync(request, status = pending, stewardId = null)
    R->>DB: INSERT EMERGENCYACCESSREQUESTS
    S->>N: NotifyAsync(every active Steward)
    STW->>W: Open pending requests
    alt approve
        W->>C: PUT /api/EmergencyAccessRequests/{id}/approve {scopeExpiresAt}
        C->>S: ApproveAsync(StewardId, Id, request)
        S->>R: Load request still pending (decided by another Steward -> 409)
        S->>R: UpdateAsync(status = approved, stewardId, decidedAt, scopeExpiresAt)
    else reject
        W->>C: PUT /api/EmergencyAccessRequests/{id}/reject {rejectionReason}
        C->>S: RejectAsync(StewardId, Id, request)
        S->>R: UpdateAsync(status = rejected, stewardId, rejectionReason)
    end
    R->>DB: UPDATE EMERGENCYACCESSREQUESTS
    S->>N: NotifyAsync(requester, decision)
    C-->>W: 200 OK
    Note over S,DB: Access ends on its own at scopeExpiresAt, every read is logged with consentPurposeId = null
